exports[`the print sheet of e27-pendant.lamp.json > matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"# E27 pendant

Print sheet · 2026-10-21 · [Open this lamp in openlamp](https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/#p=TEST)

- **Lamp:** Pendant on a cord (600 mm drop, knotted in the canopy); E27 LED bulb in a lampholder (shade ring); shade on a bayonet joint
- **Printer:** Bambu Lab A1, bed 256 × 256 × 256 mm, 0.4 mm nozzle, multi-colour (AMS lite)
- **Export:** 3 STL files, one per part, at normal quality

## Parts

| Part | Qty | Colour | PLA | Triangles | Print orientation | Joints |
| :-- | --: | :-- | --: | --: | :-- | :-- |
| Hub | 1 | warm light grey \`#d9d4cb\` | — | — | Collar ring on the bed, mount face up | bayonet for the Shade |
| Shade | 1 | cream \`#f2e8d5\` | — | — | Open end on the bed, collar up | bayonet into the Hub |
| Canopy | 1 | warm light grey \`#d9d4cb\` | — | — | Ceiling face on the bed | — |
| **Total** | **3** |  | — |  |  |  |

PLA: estimated weight of all copies; "—" until the part is built in openlamp. Triangles: of one STL.

## Also needed

- 1 × E27 lampholder with a threaded sleeve for the Ø40.5 mm hole and its shade ring
- 1 × E27 LED bulb, at most Ø60 × 110 mm (LED only: no incandescent or halogen bulbs)
- Cord Ø6 mm, at least 800 mm (the 600 mm drop and the knots) plus the run from the canopy to the power: a 2-core mains cord set with a plug and a switch (or wired to the outlet by a qualified person)
- 2 × ceiling screws up to Ø4 mm with heads up to Ø9 mm, and wall plugs, for the canopy's slots (60 mm apart)

## Assembly

1. Feed the cord down through the hub's cord boss and tie a knot that sits in the knot cavity (reach in through the hole in the hub's plate).
2. Wire the E27 lampholder to the cord (mains wiring: have it done by a qualified person), then pass its threaded sleeve through the Ø40.5 mm hole in the hub's plate and screw its shade ring on from the light face, so the plate is clamped.
3. Feed the other end of the cord up through the canopy's cord hole and tie a knot 600 mm above the hub, so it sits in the canopy's recess.
4. Screw the canopy to the ceiling through its two slots (60 mm apart) with the screws and wall plugs; connect the cable at the ceiling outlet (mains wiring: have it done by a qualified person).
5. Fit the shade to the hub: push its lugs into the slots of the hub's ring and turn it clockwise (seen from the shade's open end) until it stops.
6. Screw in an E27 LED bulb, at most Ø60 × 110 mm (LED bulbs only).

## Printing

- 0.4 mm nozzle, 0.2 mm layers (0.12 mm for finer ribs). Every part prints as exported, without supports.
- Shades: a 1.2 mm wall (3 perimeters) and no infill; a 0.8 mm wall (two 0.4 mm perimeters) diffuses the light best. White or "Jade White" PLA spreads the light most evenly.
- Print the hub in PETG: PLA softens near 60 °C, and even an LED bulb warms the hub.
- No brim (brim marks show under light): a smooth PEI plate and a slow first layer hold the thin wall.
- Exported at normal quality: draft is for quick test prints, normal is plenty for printing, fine gives smoother ribs and much larger files.

### Hub

File: \`openlamp-e27-pendant-hub.stl\`

- Print as exported: collar ring on the bed, mount face up. No supports needed.
- The lampholder's threaded sleeve goes through the Ø40.5 mm hole in the plate; screw its shade ring on from the light face, inside the skirt, so the plate is clamped.
- Feed the cord down through the boss, tie a knot that sits in the knot cavity (reach in through the plate's hole), then wire the lampholder.
- LED bulbs only. Print the hub in PETG (PLA softens near 60 °C); mains wiring is your responsibility: have it done by a qualified person.

### Shade

File: \`openlamp-e27-pendant-shade.stl\`

- Print as exported: open end on the bed, collar up. No supports needed.
- Two 0.4 mm perimeters (0.8 mm wall) diffuse the light best; no infill needed.
- Assembly: push the shade's lugs up into the hub's slots and turn the shade clockwise (seen from below) until it stops.

### Canopy

File: \`openlamp-e27-pendant-canopy.stl\`

- Print as exported: ceiling face on the bed. No supports needed.
- Feed the cord up through the canopy and tie a knot that sits in the recess; then screw the canopy to the ceiling through its two slots.

## Warnings

- ℹ E27 bulb: LED bulbs only (no incandescent or halogen bulbs); print the hub in PETG (PLA softens near 60 °C), and have the mains wiring done by a qualified person.
- ℹ canopy does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.
- ℹ hub does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.

---

Made with openlamp, https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/
"
`;

