exports[`the print sheet of lattice-drum.lamp.json > matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"# Lattice drum

Print sheet · 2026-10-21 · [Open this lamp in openlamp](https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/#p=TEST)

- **Lamp:** Pendant on a cord (600 mm drop, knotted in the canopy); USB LED puck (Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001, Ø59 × 8 mm); shade on a bayonet joint
- **Printer:** Bambu Lab A1, bed 256 × 256 × 256 mm, 0.4 mm nozzle, multi-colour (AMS lite)
- **Export:** 3 STL files, one per part, at normal quality

## Parts

| Part | Qty | Colour | PLA | Triangles | Print orientation | Joints |
| :-- | --: | :-- | --: | --: | :-- | :-- |
| Hub | 1 | dark grey \`#2b2b2e\` | — | — | Collar ring on the bed, mount face up | bayonet for the Shade |
| Shade | 1 | dark grey \`#2b2b2e\` | — | — | Open end on the bed, collar up | bayonet into the Hub |
| Canopy | 1 | dark grey \`#2b2b2e\` | — | — | Ceiling face on the bed | — |
| **Total** | **3** |  | — |  |  |  |

PLA: estimated weight of all copies; "—" until the part is built in openlamp. Triangles: of one STL.

## Also needed

- 1 × USB LED puck: Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001 (Ø59 × 8 mm) or any puck of that size, with its USB cable
- 1 × USB power adapter (5 V)
- Cord Ø4 mm, at least 800 mm (the 600 mm drop and the knots) plus the run from the canopy to the power: the puck's USB cable or a USB extension
- 2 × ceiling screws up to Ø4 mm with heads up to Ø9 mm, and wall plugs, for the canopy's slots (60 mm apart)

## Assembly

1. Feed the cord down through the hub's cord boss, pull it out through the light opening, tie a knot and pull it back up into the knot cavity.
2. Press the LED puck into the hub from the light face until it stops; the crush ribs hold it.
3. Feed the other end of the cord up through the canopy's cord hole and tie a knot 600 mm above the hub, so it sits in the canopy's recess.
4. Screw the canopy to the ceiling through its two slots (60 mm apart) with the screws and wall plugs; run the cable on to the power supply.
5. Fit the shade to the hub: push its lugs into the slots of the hub's ring and turn it clockwise (seen from the shade's open end) until it stops.

## Printing

- 0.4 mm nozzle, 0.2 mm layers (0.12 mm for finer ribs). Every part prints as exported, without supports.
- Shades: a 1.2 mm wall (3 perimeters) and no infill; a 0.8 mm wall (two 0.4 mm perimeters) diffuses the light best. White or "Jade White" PLA spreads the light most evenly.
- No brim (brim marks show under light): a smooth PEI plate and a slow first layer hold the thin wall.
- Exported at normal quality: draft is for quick test prints, normal is plenty for printing, fine gives smoother ribs and much larger files.

### Hub

File: \`openlamp-lattice-drum-hub.stl\`

- Print as exported: collar ring on the bed, mount face up. No supports needed.
- Feed the cord down through the boss, pull it out through the light opening, tie a knot and pull it back up into the knot cavity; then press the puck in from below until it stops (crush ribs hold it).

### Shade

File: \`openlamp-lattice-drum-shade.stl\`

- Print as exported: open end on the bed, collar up. The holes print without supports (hexagons point up, round holes bridge their short tops).
- Two 0.4 mm perimeters (0.8 mm wall) diffuse the light best; no infill needed.
- Assembly: push the shade's lugs up into the hub's slots and turn the shade clockwise (seen from below) until it stops.

### Canopy

File: \`openlamp-lattice-drum-canopy.stl\`

- Print as exported: ceiling face on the bed. No supports needed.
- Feed the cord up through the canopy and tie a knot that sits in the recess; then screw the canopy to the ceiling through its two slots.

## Warnings

- ℹ canopy does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.

---

Made with openlamp, https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/
"
`;

