"# Table lamp

Print sheet · 2026-10-21 · [Open this lamp in openlamp](https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/#p=TEST)

- **Lamp:** Table lamp (400 mm stem in 2 segments); USB LED puck (Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001, Ø59 × 8 mm); shade on a bayonet joint
- **Printer:** Bambu Lab A1, bed 256 × 256 × 256 mm, 0.4 mm nozzle, multi-colour (AMS lite)
- **Export:** 6 STL files, one per part, at normal quality

## Parts

| Part | Qty | Colour | PLA | Triangles | Print orientation | Joints |
| :-- | --: | :-- | --: | --: | :-- | :-- |
| Hub | 1 | warm light grey \`#d9d4cb\` | — | — | Collar ring on the bed, mount face up | bayonet for the Shade; thread Ø20 × 2.5 for the Stem segment |
| Shade | 1 | cream \`#f1e6d2\` | — | — | Open end on the bed, collar up | bayonet into the Hub |
| Stem segment | 1 | dark grey \`#3a3835\` | — | — | Female thread on the bed, male thread up | thread Ø20 × 2.5 into the Hub; thread Ø20 × 2.5 for the Stem foot |
| Stem foot | 1 | dark grey \`#3a3835\` | — | — | Flange on the bed, thread up | thread Ø20 × 2.5 into the Stem segment; 4 × M3 into the Base |
| Base | 1 | dark grey \`#3a3835\` | — | — | Top face on the bed, weight pocket and cable groove up | 4 × M3 (heat-set inserts) for the Stem foot |
| Base lid | 1 | dark grey \`#3a3835\` | — | — | Flat, the side that faces into the pocket on the bed | — |
| **Total** | **6** |  | — |  |  |  |

PLA: estimated weight of all copies; "—" until the part is built in openlamp. Triangles: of one STL.

## Also needed

- 1 × USB LED puck: Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001 (Ø59 × 8 mm) or any puck of that size, with its USB cable
- 1 × USB power adapter (5 V)
- Weight for the base: about 1 kg of steel shot (or 370 g of dry sand, or washers) to fill the pocket
- Cable Ø6 mm, at least 750 mm through the stem and out of the base plus the run to the power: the puck's USB cable or a USB extension
- 4 × M3 × 8 screws (Stem foot to Base)
- 4 × M3 heat-set inserts (and a soldering iron to set them)

## Assembly

1. Press four M3 heat-set inserts into the pockets in the base's top face.
2. Turn the base over, fill the weight pocket with about 1 kg of steel shot (or 370 g of dry sand) and close it with the lid: press it in, notch over the spoke; the crush ribs hold it.
3. Screw the stem foot's flange onto the base with four M3 × 8 screws.
4. Feed the cable up through the base and the stem foot, then through each stem segment, screwing each onto the one below (clockwise seen from above) until the shoulders meet.
5. Press the LED puck into the hub from the light face until it stops (the crush ribs hold it); its cable runs through the bore in the hub's mount face.
6. Screw the hub onto the top of the stem, clockwise seen from above.
7. Fit the shade to the hub: push its lugs into the slots of the hub's ring and turn it clockwise (seen from the shade's open end) until it stops.
8. Lay the cable in the groove under the base and out through the notch in its rim.

## Printing

- 0.4 mm nozzle, 0.2 mm layers (0.12 mm for finer ribs). Every part prints as exported, without supports.
- Shades: a 0.8 mm wall (2 perimeters), which diffuses the light best, and no infill. White or "Jade White" PLA spreads the light most evenly.
- No brim (brim marks show under light): a smooth PEI plate and a slow first layer hold the thin wall.
- Exported at normal quality: draft is for quick test prints, normal is plenty for printing, fine gives smoother ribs and much larger files.

### Hub

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-hub.stl\`

- Print as exported: collar ring on the bed, mount face up. No supports needed.
- Press the puck in from below until it stops (crush ribs hold it); its cable runs up through the bore in the mount face.

### Shade

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-shade.stl\`

- Print as exported: open end on the bed, collar up. No supports needed.
- Two 0.4 mm perimeters (0.8 mm wall) diffuse the light best; no infill needed.
- Assembly: push the shade's lugs up into the hub's slots and turn the shade clockwise (seen from below) until it stops.

### Stem segment

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-stem.stl\`

- Print as exported: female thread on the bed, male thread up. No supports needed.
- Assembly: feed the cable through the segments, then screw each one onto the one below, clockwise seen from above, until the shoulders meet.

### Stem foot

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-stemFoot.stl\`

- Print as exported: flange on the bed, thread up. No supports needed.
- Screw the flange onto the base with 4 M3 × 8 screws; the heads sit on the flange.

### Base

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-base.stl\`

- Print as exported: top face on the bed, weight pocket and cable groove up. No supports needed.
- Fill the pocket with steel shot, washers or sand, close it with the lid, and lay the cable in the groove under the base, out through the notch in the rim.
- Press 4 M3 heat-set inserts into the pockets in the top face.

### Base lid

File: \`openlamp-table-lamp-baseLid.stl\`

- Print as exported: flat, the side that faces into the pocket on the bed.
- Press the lid into the pocket's mouth, notch over the spoke; the three crush ribs hold it.

## Warnings

- ℹ base does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.
- ℹ baseLid does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.
- ℹ hub does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.
- ℹ stemFoot does not fit on the same plate as the other parts; print it separately.

---

Made with openlamp, https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/
"
`;

