"# Trumpet

Print sheet · 2026-10-21 · [Open this lamp in openlamp](https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/#p=TEST)

- **Lamp:** Velcro strap on the ceiling; USB LED puck (Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001, Ø59 × 8 mm); hub and shade printed as one piece
- **Printer:** Bambu Lab A1, bed 256 × 256 × 256 mm, 0.4 mm nozzle, multi-colour (AMS lite)
- **Export:** 1 STL file, at normal quality

## Parts

| Part | Qty | Colour | PLA | Triangles | Print orientation | Joints |
| :-- | --: | :-- | --: | --: | :-- | :-- |
| Shade (fused) | 1 | warm white \`#f4efe6\` | — | — | Open end on the bed, housing on top | — |
| **Total** | **1** |  | — |  |  |  |

PLA: estimated weight of all copies; "—" until the part is built in openlamp. Triangles: of one STL.

## Also needed

- 1 × USB LED puck: Bambu Lab LED Lamp Kit-001 (Ø59 × 8 mm) or any puck of that size, with its USB cable
- 1 × USB power adapter (5 V)
- 1 × self-adhesive velcro (hook-and-loop) strip for the ceiling, at least 25 × 66 mm
- 1 × strip of the mating velcro, 25 mm wide and about 130 mm long (trim the tails)

## Assembly

1. Stick the self-adhesive hook strip (or the loop strip, either way round) to the ceiling.
2. Drop the LED puck into the pocket from the top, diffuser facing down into the shade, and lay its cable out through the slot in the housing wall.
3. Thread a strip of the mating velcro down through one side tunnel, across the top of the housing (over the back of the puck) and down through the other tunnel. The strap keeps the puck in; trim the tails.
4. Press the lamp against the ceiling strip. To take it down, peel it off.

## Printing

- 0.4 mm nozzle, 0.2 mm layers (0.12 mm for finer ribs). Every part prints as exported, without supports.
- Shades: a 0.8 mm wall (2 perimeters), which diffuses the light best, and no infill. White or "Jade White" PLA spreads the light most evenly.
- No brim (brim marks show under light): a smooth PEI plate and a slow first layer hold the thin wall.
- Exported at normal quality: draft is for quick test prints, normal is plenty for printing, fine gives smoother ribs and much larger files.

### Shade (fused)

File: \`openlamp-trumpet-shade.stl\`

- Print as exported: open end on the bed, housing on top. No supports needed.
- Two 0.4 mm perimeters (0.8 mm wall) diffuse the light best; no infill needed.

## Warnings

None.

---

Made with openlamp, https://jahoefne.github.io/openlamp/
"
`;

